 known as a freshman is  that being a Hillsdale ian requires  humility and a lot of it we are here to  learn which means that we might have to  admit that we don't know everything that  we may be wrong at times and that's okay  there's a sign that you passed as you  drive into town it reads Hillsdale it's  the people i laughed the first time I  read it but it didn't take me long to  realize how true that sign is Hillsdale  really is all about the people dr.  Whalen once said the conversation of all  is a series of lectures to each what  does that mean it means we need to stop  trying to prove ourselves and instead  listen and learn because we are  surrounded by some of the greatest minds  in our nation so we can't let our  education stop at the doorway of the  classroom we must engage ourselves in  lunch discussions because that's where  some of our greatest learning occurs we  can't just try to justify our own  beliefs but instead we must humble  ourselves and be willing to hear other  people out willing to be wrong willing  to swallow our pride and shift our views  because being a Hillsdale ian means you  do whatever it takes to pursue truth  I've also learned that being a Hillsdale  ian means effort is everything I  remember being terrified my first few  weeks here that I was going to fail  every single class I was in but I've  learned that if you put the effort in  you'll get the results out yes this  school is rigorous but you're up for the  challenge you wouldn't have applied if  you weren't let alone have been accepted  Colossians 3 23 says whatever you do  work heartily as for the Lord not for  men  that verse has been an encouragement and  an anthem for me at Hillsdale I've  learned that not everyone catches on to  concepts at the same pace some of us  have to put in more hours than other  people in order to understand something  it takes me a lot longer to write a  paper I will get the job done but it can  seem like it takes me three times longer  than some of my friends but here's the  truth we all learn differently so don't  fall into the comparison trap don't get  caught up comparing yourself to others  don't obsess on your weaknesses but  invest in your strengths being a  Hillsdale Ian means you know that hard  work and a willing spirit can take you  anywhere regardless of where you're  starting from lastly I've learned that  being a Hillsdale Ian means you are  constantly challenging yourself I once  heard it said to be outstanding get  comfortable with being uncomfortable I  have a personal mantra that is along the  same lines I tell myself if it doesn't  scare you it's not big enough and I have  to tell myself this often obviously we  do not want to live our lives in the  confines of fear but at the same time a  little bit of fear is a healthy thing it  keeps you on your toes it pushes you to  do more and to be more I believe that if  you're not being stretched then you're  not growing go to office hours with that  Professor that you feel completely  intimidated by take one class each  semester that scares you s TS Eliot said  if you're not in over your head how do  you know how tall you are don't let your  fear paralyze you let it inspire you  because it means you're stretching  yourself you're growing you'll never be  ready if you keep waiting to be so when  it's negative 20 degrees out and you're  trekking to your 8am  you're a Hillsdale Ian you've got this  when it's 3am and you still haven't  finished your 15 page research paper due  the next day remember you're a Hillsdale  Ian you've got this parents when your  child hugs you today and says goodbye  look them in the eye and remind them you  are a Hillsdale Ian you've got this when  facing the impossible task the  incomprehensible thought the infeasible  situation always remember you're a  Hillsdale Ian you've got this today you  all become Hillsdale Ian's and you get  to devote the next four years to  studying how to live and love well to  consider the 